{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2634 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "554d819a230582f2d800c1ba672355c0e06dc8b8f874157ec882d2eedef54720" :edb/db-before-t 2633 :edb/db-after-t 2634 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535946 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:12:57.644Z" 13194139535946 true] [17592186192606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375898 13194139535946 true] [17592186192606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375912 13194139535946 true] [17592186192606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375919 13194139535946 true] [17592186192607 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375905 13194139535946 true] [17592186193146 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535946 true] [17592186193146 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070328/assets/df3b62554600601401d14d3b6758a3c350cf8cddc3788e79a3ba456a5a19c60a.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$" 13194139535946 true] [17592186193146 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4077/Source/Images/q-35595.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of $R^{2}$ or $R^{3}$?" 13194139535946 false] [17592186193146 1145 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents the origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,,\\,$ which is considered a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375899 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1089 "q-110761" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $A={⟨2t,2+t⟩\\,:\\,t\\in R}$\n- $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=1}$" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1113 #uuid "d189a361-c4b6-51b0-8803-3d2da2828666" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375898 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have, for some $t$:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 2+t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t=0 \\\\ 2+t=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the system has no solution. So, $0$ is not in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace.  It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x-y=0$ since $0-0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $y=1$ since $0\\ne 1.$ So, $0$ is not in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375900 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375901 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375902 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375903 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375904 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1041 "selection" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375904 13194139535946 true] [17592186375899 1110 #uuid "937c088a-c3b6-5cb8-aaa4-2226b64c1b21" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375900 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375900 1111 #uuid "3601edf3-7bc3-5e47-9192-e196ae0e963b" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375901 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375901 1111 #uuid "6e0da404-720d-5418-b847-1a43cc313cda" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375902 1034 "I only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375902 1111 #uuid "5b6e3c0a-30bc-59bd-bd90-15f5376494ba" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375903 1034 "III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375903 1111 #uuid "e76f095c-d497-5e72-9442-303c5e7a57be" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375904 1034 "II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375904 1111 #uuid "20e3bf36-2efb-5912-9b29-2abb28d142a8" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375906 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1089 "q-158100" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070328/assets/003b4f77a413444989bcec8b9682465419a58ded55ed95cefb4f43c122bdc3d3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1113 #uuid "1cf36aea-1a3d-5f57-9970-f75b927a4791" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375905 1145 "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram I is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents the origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,,\\,$ which is considered a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375907 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375908 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375909 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375910 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375911 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1041 "selection" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375911 13194139535946 true] [17592186375906 1110 #uuid "648718ce-02cf-59fe-b2ff-5e8c18a6da25" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375907 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375907 1111 #uuid "15b102c6-52d8-5b4b-b89e-5d649a149a3e" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375908 1034 "I only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375908 1111 #uuid "7b09d73f-7b77-5e95-8991-6ca5a8971844" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375909 1034 "III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375909 1111 #uuid "e7c23ad4-a08f-5509-8889-af165b8c63cf" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375910 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375910 1111 #uuid "3f421a8d-15cc-5f11-a51f-88d9ddfdee23" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375911 1034 "II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375911 1111 #uuid "68c0ce32-21f4-5e2b-a162-ea78eefd6a8a" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375913 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1089 "q-34327" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0}$\n- $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=2y}$\n- $C={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1113 #uuid "01166beb-7893-5365-92e5-cedbd35f370b" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375912 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. It actually represents the whole space ${R}^{2}$, since the coordinates of any vector $⟨x,y⟩$ satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=2y$ since $0=2\\cdot 0.$ So, $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. It also represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x-y=0$ since $0-0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $C.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375914 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375915 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375916 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375917 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375918 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1041 "selection" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375914 13194139535946 true] [17592186375913 1110 #uuid "8e3acf2d-2323-55af-8e64-c9950a843dff" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375914 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375914 1111 #uuid "af5c3b1d-8dac-5923-80f7-00e4eca77470" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375915 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375915 1111 #uuid "6d9bb4c9-850c-5b6b-8168-665b8168e88e" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375916 1034 "I only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375916 1111 #uuid "acf6188f-68a6-59e7-b380-812cad7e20af" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375917 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375917 1111 #uuid "037018be-1f69-578f-881d-2975ecfdb3bc" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375918 1034 "II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375918 1111 #uuid "feffaf29-adc3-5373-ae58-c9ef05a5b1df" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375920 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1089 "q-74255" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1100 "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}<\\frac{1}{2}}$\n- $B={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:5x-y-z=0}$\n- $C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:5-x-z=0}$" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1113 #uuid "0f2b0a81-556c-5bc3-bde3-5b6da6eef31a" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375919 1145 "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace. Indeed, the vector $u=⟨\\frac{1}{4},0,0⟩$ is in $A$, since\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}<\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nbut, $4u=⟨1,0,0⟩$ is not in $B$, since \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}>\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, $A$ is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $5x-y-z=0$ since $5\\cdot 0-0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $5-x-z=0$ since $5-0-0\\ne 0.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375921 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375922 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375923 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375924 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375925 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1041 "selection" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375925 13194139535946 true] [17592186375920 1110 #uuid "cc864d67-6e0c-5113-a4a0-7632b4715c9b" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375921 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375921 1111 #uuid "47b35ff3-1d83-5ca1-bcc4-f15101f4d50b" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375922 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375922 1111 #uuid "7b2e92a6-3564-5527-a3ad-41c7c6f38ab6" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375923 1034 "I only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375923 1111 #uuid "37b7346d-c46a-50b1-8651-20de4ac00c35" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375924 1034 "III only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375924 1111 #uuid "7c8216c6-9bed-5449-b02a-cd20fd7f1fee" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375925 1034 "II only" 13194139535946 true] [17592186375925 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535946 true] [17592186375925 1111 #uuid "85bd939b-cea6-5d54-89c8-be44f4c1141f" 13194139535946 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-110761" 17592186375898 "q-110761/selection" 17592186375899 "q-110761/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186375900 "q-110761/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186375901 "q-110761/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d